{"article_ids": ["3d2697b636d74b83"], "canonical_title": "Building on Nemotron 3.5 Parse: Open Data, Fine-Tuning, and Faster Inference", "category": "infrastructure", "confidence": 0.4, "description": "Hugging Face announced a new offering built on the Nemotron 3.5 Parse model that provides open data, supports fine‑tuning, and delivers faster inference.", "entities": ["model:nemotron", "model:nemotron-3.5"], "first_seen": "2026-11-26T05:05:36Z", "id": "evt_3d2697b636d74b83", "importance_score": 6.422, "last_updated": "2026-11-26T05:05:36Z", "source_ids": ["huggingface-blog"]}
{"article_ids": ["17bcad2e36d06ce8"], "canonical_title": "KiRA: Kronecker Input-Gated Rank Adaptation for Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning of Pretrained Models", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper presents KiRA, a new PEFT technique that uses Kronecker‑based input‑gated rank adaptation to vary the low‑rank update capacity per input, addressing the limitation that existing PEFT methods keep a fixed rank across all inputs.", "entities": ["term:peft"], "first_seen": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_17bcad2e36d06ce8", "importance_score": 6.19, "last_updated": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
{"article_ids": ["557aca624a23055f"], "canonical_title": "EVA: Evidence-seeking Visual Agent for Hallucination-Resistant Multimodal Reasoning", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper presents EVA, an Evidence‑seeking Visual Agent designed to reduce hallucinations in multimodal large language models (MLLMs). It identifies that hallucinations often stem from unchecked visual assumptions and that self‑reflection, multi‑agent debate, or counterfactual verification can amplify errors when they rely on the same faulty assumptions. EVA leverages external visual tools to obtain verifiable evidence, aiming to select appropriate tools, supply correct parameters, and incorporate the evidence into the model's reasoning process.", "entities": ["term:eva"], "first_seen": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_557aca624a23055f", "importance_score": 6.14, "last_updated": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["cc44d5e0e57b06ca"], "canonical_title": "FCC signs off on SpaceX’s plan to put up to 1 million data center satellites into space", "category": "infrastructure", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "The U.S. Federal Communications Commission granted SpaceX authorization to launch up to one million satellites equipped with AI chips as part of its \"Starmind\" initiative, marking the first regulatory approval for a space‑based AI data‑center concept. The filing notes that other companies, such as Google and Blue Origin, are also exploring similar satellite AI data‑center ideas.", "entities": ["org:google", "term:fcc"], "first_seen": "2026-11-25T17:44:51Z", "id": "evt_cc44d5e0e57b06ca", "importance_score": 5.867, "last_updated": "2026-11-25T17:44:51Z", "source_ids": ["the-verge-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["c74ed50124d17eea"], "canonical_title": "Focus On Facts: Stylistically Invariant and Factually Sensitive Text Embeddings", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Researchers identified that standard text embedding models often prioritize surface-form similarity over factual identity, preferring altered near‑copies with corrupted facts over fact‑preserving rewrites. They introduced hard‑negative contrastive supervision to mitigate this shortcut and created FOF‑Bench, an 83,263‑triplet benchmark covering five domains to evaluate factual sensitivity of embeddings.", "entities": ["term:fof"], "first_seen": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_c74ed50124d17eea", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-11-26T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
